      "htmlSolution": "<p><span style=\"font-style: italic; font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 9pt;\">a) </span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 10pt;\">  1.Qa3-d6 Rg6*g5 [+wBg6]   2.Bg6-e4 + Rg5-d5 # </span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-style: italic; font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 9pt;\">b) bBg6 </span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 10pt;\">  1.Qa3-a6 Bg6*h5 [+wRg6]   2.Rg6-g8 + Bh5-e8 # </span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-style: italic; font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 9pt;\">3rd Prize G.Brunori: creation of different black batteries from pinned white pieces in </span></p><p><span style=\"font-style: italic; font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 9pt;\">both phases; the pin mates enphasize the fairy strategy and the exchange of function </span></p><p><span style=\"font-style: italic; font-family: &quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;; font-size: 9pt;\">of black and white pieces.</span></p><p></p><p></p>",
